From: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 23:04:37 +0200
Subject: riscv: dts: sophgo: run the Milk-V Duo S eMMC at HS200

The Duo S eMMC has been held at high speed by no-1-8-v, which on a 4-bit bus
caps it at about 22 MB/s. The card offers HS200 (EXT_CSD DEVICE_TYPE 0x57),
the controller advertises SDR104, and the vendor stack runs it that way: its
U-Boot is built without MMC_IO_VOLTAGE, so mmc_set_lowest_voltage() is a stub
and it tunes into HS200 without touching any supply, and its kernel gives the
eMMC host an empty voltage_switch hook.

Mainline does the same once no-1-8-v is gone. There is no vqmmc supply, so
sdhci_start_signal_voltage_switch() only sets VDD_180 in HOST_CONTROL2 and
reads it back, and cv18xx_sdhci_execute_tuning() finds the sampling phase.
The pads stay on VDDIO_EMMC, the 3.3V rail - HS200 on 3.3V I/O is outside what
JEDEC specifies, and it is what the board ships with.

An earlier attempt at this left the card unenumerated, and the eMMC pad patch
recorded that as the reason to keep no-1-8-v. It was not the mode: a 7.0 boot
from the same week, with a different device tree, reports "new HS200 MMC card",
and the tree now enumerates it every time.

Measured on a Duo S (8GTF4R, 7.28 GiB), page cache dropped before each run,
1 GiB raw read and 512 MiB written including sync:

  high speed   46.9 MHz   22 MB/s read   18 MB/s write
  HS200       187.5 MHz   84 MB/s read   47 MB/s write

512 MiB of random data written and read back matched, a reference file written
in high speed read back intact, and dmesg showed no mmc or I/O errors. Card
init takes about 0.75 s longer, for the tuning.

DDR52 at 3.3V (mmc-ddr-3_3v) was tried as the in-spec alternative and is not
usable here: reads work, and every write fails with an I/O error.

Signed-off-by: Armbian <info@armbian.com>
---
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duo-s.dts
@@ -186,9 +186,18 @@ &pinctrl {
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * HS200, so no no-1-8-v. There is no 1.8V to switch to - VDDIO_EMMC is the
+ * 3.3V rail, see the pad group above - and none is needed: with no vqmmc supply
+ * the switch only sets VDD_180 in HOST_CONTROL2 and reads it back. The vendor
+ * kernel's eMMC voltage_switch hook is empty and its bootloader tunes into
+ * HS200 the same way; HS200 on 3.3V I/O is outside what JEDEC specifies, and
+ * is what this board ships with. On a Duo S it tunes at 187.5 MHz and reads at
+ * 84 MB/s against 22 MB/s in high speed. DDR52 at 3.3V (mmc-ddr-3_3v), the
+ * in-spec alternative, fails every write.
+ */
 &emmc {
 	bus-width = <4>;
-	no-1-8-v;
 	cap-mmc-hw-reset;
 	no-sd;
 	no-sdio;
-- 
